I’d like to talk about a drink that I learned to prepare, which is Vietnamese egg coffee.

I learned how to make it about a year ago when I was spending more time at home during a long holiday. Since I’m a huge coffee lover, I became curious about how this famous Vietnamese drink is made. I learned it in my kitchen after watching several tutorial videos on YouTube and TikTok.

At first, I thought it would be quite simple, but it actually required a bit of patience and attention to detail. The most difficult part was whisking the egg mixture properly so that it became smooth and creamy without having a strong egg smell. After a few failed attempts, I finally managed to make a cup that tasted surprisingly good.

What I really enjoyed about learning to make egg coffee was the sense of satisfaction it gave me. It also became a relaxing activity that helped me reduce stress after work. Since then, I’ve occasionally made it for my friends and family, and they were quite impressed by it.

Overall, I think learning how to prepare this drink was both enjoyable and rewarding because it allowed me to appreciate Vietnamese coffee culture even more.
